    {
      "ordinal": 3,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "1.1",
      "title": "Definition and general requirements",
      "body": "● A competitor must have a belt flag with your number on it that identifies you\n● A competitor may have a second belt flag that is decorative symbols and decorations used for this must be based on historical sources. Any clearly modern symbol or decoration is denied.\n● No more than two belt flags may be worn by a competitor Examples: Warhammer logo, movies or TV show imagery, modern slogan etc\n● Belt flag is an element hung on a belt designed to show your belt number in the list.\n● Belt flag must be made of fabric or leather.\n● Belt flag must conform with the Textiles and Leather rules document.\n● Belt flag consists of a base and a number.\n● Base must respect the following requirements:\n○ Base shape can be square, rectangular or triangular.\n○ Base must have a trim to be worn with a belt.\n○ Base must be made of one main color.\n○ Some decoration can be added on the edges of the base.\n○ Such decoration must not interfere with the readability of the belt flag.\n● Number must respect the following requirements:\n○ Individual figures must be from 0 to 9.\n○ Numbers must be from 01 to 99.\n○ Number must be written in Arabic numerals.\n○ Number must be 13 cm tall as a minimum.\n○ Number can be of any color, contrasting with the base main color.\n● All Belt flags must respect the following dimensions:\n○ Length: from 26 cm to 36 cm.\n○ Width: from 14 cm to 18 cm.",
